    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on **Isaac Paredes** and **Corbin Carroll** today. **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) carries our highest projection, benefiting from a soft matchup against Klassen (6.12 xERA); his ability to capitalize on a high-xERA starter provides a massive ceiling in the RBI and HR categories. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** (66.31) remains a primary focal point for our stolen base strategy. Despite a neutral matchup against Suarez, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-efficiency environment, bolstered by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which significantly increases his upside for a stolen base. **Mickey Moniak** (65.81) is our surprise riser; while his platoon splits against Lauer are typically a concern, the extreme park factors and the pitcher\u2019s projected vulnerability elevate his profile to a \"Strong\" start, making him an essential component of the daily stack.\n\nThe decision to bench **Vinnie Pasquantino** (43.58) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he sits above our 40-point floor, he was edged out by the more favorable situational metrics of **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley**. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is hamstrung by a sub-optimal platoon matchup against the left-handed Basso, which suppresses his projection relative to the rest of the infield. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (61.42) earns a spot not just for his raw power, but for the situational green light against Matthews; his specific BvP indicators and the opportunity to exploit a pitcher who is susceptible to base-stealing catchers provide more multifaceted utility than the pure power profile of **Vinnie Pasquantino**.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Griffin Conine** (41.74) closely. While he clears the minimum threshold, he faces a significant hurdle in Wheeler (3.02 xERA) and an elite defensive catcher who limits the stolen base upside of the entire lineup. Given the high stakes of this Roto stretch, keep a close watch on **Henry Bolte** (55.27); his top-of-the-order positioning against Lynch IV gives him significant volume leverage that could outperform his base projection. Ensure you are ready to pivot if early weather reports for the later games suggest any deterioration in conditions, as we cannot afford empty plate appearances in our quest to close the gap in the SB standings.",
